{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfKxZbBoPvhjrfsgE4Deq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is expected behavior — it's not really a Prettier plugin bug, it's inherent to how Tailwind treats dynamic strings.\n\nPer `src/docs/detecting-classes-in-source-files.mdx` (§ \"Dynamic class names\", line 67): *\"Since Tailwind scans your source files as plain text, it has no way of understanding string concatenation or interpolation in the programming language you're using.\"*\n\nEach segment between `${...}` interpolations is treated as an independent plain-text chunk, so the sorter (and Tailwind's scanner in general) can only reorder classes within a segment, not across the interpolation boundary. This isn't documented specifically for `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss`, but it follows the same plain-text scanning model."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":426,"cache_read_input_tokens":13263,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":426},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a55c1f7-6df4-493f-b1e7-1b057d6f44e1","uuid":"eacc5f2c-770e-4b82-b022-4faee3d6af60","timestamp":"2026-09-23T07:14:47.936Z","request_id":"req_011CfKxZabKfWzLYtyxi239p"}
